From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 11:52:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the loaded creature counts as a running total

SpawnerCreature asked, once per creature type on every tick of every
world, for the sum of chunk.entityCount over every loaded chunk - and
PandaSpigot answered it by walking the whole chunk map. With a few
thousand chunks loaded that is a few thousand hash lookups four times a
tick, and a live capture put it at 5.2% of the main thread during chunk
generation.

ChunkCreatureCensus mirrors that sum incrementally. It keys on the
creature Class rather than on EnumCreatureType, so it tracks whatever
Chunk.entityCount tracks even if two creature types ever shared a class.
It is maintained at the five places the provider's chunk map is mutated,
and wherever Chunk adjusts a count for a chunk that is currently in that
map.

The four counts are still read one at a time. Precomputing them together
would be wrong: entities spawned during one creature type's pass are
visible to the next pass's count today, and a plugin reacting to the
spawn can add anything at all.

Whether every call site was found is not something a unit test can see,
so debugVerifyAthenaIndexes now rebuilds the sum from every loaded chunk
each tick and compares. Summoning and killing 72 entities across all
four creature types over 5400 audited ticks reported no divergence;
deleting one of the two adjustment calls and repeating produced 1180
mismatches naming the exact class and the exact drift, so the check is
one that can fail.

ChunkCreatureCensusTest covers the container itself, including that a
count returning to zero is forgotten rather than left as a zero entry -
otherwise every audit tick would report a difference that is not there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

